# AI integration rules

## Provider layer

`src/lib/ai/openrouter.ts` is the only place the OpenRouter client is constructed.

- Read `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and `OPENROUTER_MODEL` from server env
- Fallback model: `openrouter/free` if unset
- Return content plus model metadata (`requestedModel`, `model`, `durationMs`)
- Log every call via `src/lib/ai/logger.ts`
- Never hardcode API keys or ship secrets to the client

## Prompts

- Builders live in `src/lib/ai/prompts.ts`:
  `createPlannerPrompt`, `createPlanImprovementPrompt`, `createWriterPrompt`,
  `createVerifierPrompt`
- Keep depth limits: quick ≤ 3, standard ≤ 5, deep ≤ 8 sections
- Ask for JSON only; validate with helpers before responding

## API routes

Implement/maintain:

- `POST /api/ai/plan`
- `POST /api/ai/improve-plan`
- `POST /api/ai/write`
- `POST /api/ai/verify`

Each route must validate input, call OpenRouter securely, handle errors, and return
structured JSON with optional `meta` (model, duration, preview).

## Structured output

- Prefer JSON mode, with safe parse + non-JSON fallback retry
- Never trust raw model text without schema/normalization checks
- On invalid JSON, return a clean API error — do not crash the UI

## Logging

Server terminal and UI activity log should show:

- which operation ran (`plan` / `write` / `verify`…)
- which model OpenRouter actually used
- success vs error
- latency and a short preview of successful output

## Forbidden

- Calling OpenRouter from React client components
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_` AI secrets
- Generating entire multi-section reports in one giant request (write section-by-section)
